WEBVTT

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.480
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.690
Welcome!

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.200
<i>Welcome!</i>

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>Welcome to Tingaara!</i>

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.280
This is taking forever.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.580
There are so many kinds of fish. 
That's why.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.460
You look like you're in the
shichi-go-san festival.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.380
Shut up. So do you.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.250
I'm surprised, though.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.600
I didn't think you'd work at Tingaara, too.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.160
Your gramps introduced me.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.880
And the conditions were better 
than other places.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:26.730
Hello!

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.940
New hires!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.110
I've been waiting to see you.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:34.410
You're going to be members 
of Tingaara going forward.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.670
Work hard.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.220
I have high hopes for you.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.120
Yes, sir.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.720
I'm going to hand out your official
appointment forms in order.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.190
Nakamura Kai-kun.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.150
Yes, sir.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.140
I assign you as an Attendant 
in charge of fish.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.540
Misakino Kukuru-san.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.210
Yes, sir.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.960
I assign you to Project PR 
in the marketing department.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.970
<b>Assignment</b>

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.970
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.970
<b>As of April 1, 2022, you are assigned 
to Project PR in Marketing.</b>

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.490
<b>Project PR in Marketing</b>

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.490
Project PR in Marketing...

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.660
Marketing here.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.670
Unfortunately, they're not...

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.450
Yes, thank you.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.860
The animals...

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.750
There are no animals...

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.210
Hey, now, what are you doing?

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.720
K-Karin-chan!

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.410
Help me, Karin-chan!

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.790
I have no idea what's going on.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.480
They've got the wrong person!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.240
I'm not in marketing!

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.680
I'm an attendant!

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.470
That director must have gotten 
his Japanese wrong!

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:18.780
Here.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.600
This is your seat, Kukuru.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:25.870
I'm in marketing, too, working on sales
promotion and product development.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.370
I look forward to working with you.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.460
You're with me, huh?

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.060
I am, but we're doing different work.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.150
Tingaara's a big aquarium.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.910
There's more than one department.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.250
Broadly speaking, there's the
attendant team, the facilities team,

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.310
and the marketing team that we're in.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.290
Even though we're both in marketing, 
you're on projects and PR, so—

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.680
Crap, I need to get going.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.160
Maeda-san, could you do me a favor 
and copy these?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:53.890
<b>New Gift Shop Products</b>

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:53.890
<b>Project Proposal</b>

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.490
Okay!

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.580
See you later, Kukuru.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:03.610
Nice to meet you.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.860
I'm Maeda Akari. 
I work part-time in the office.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.840
Nice to meet you.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.950
You have such glowing cheeks!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.670
You're so adorable!

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.250
Hello.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.590
Hello.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.090
Are you the new hire?

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.780
Misakino Kukuru.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.060
I look forward to working with you!

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.790
Assistant Director Suwa.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.010
Since we just opened, 
we have no staff trainers.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.100
I've been assigned to instruct you.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.440
I've asked for backup, but it'll
be just the two of us for a while.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:43.200
The director told me 
we'd be getting experienced, talented people.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.900
It doesn't look that way to me.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.160
I've been an attendant—

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.990
At that aquarium 
that's always been in the red?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.560
An aquarium is nothing without its guests.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.420
There's no future for a facility 
that can't operate healthily.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.420
But Gama Gama—

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.960
Became dilapidated and closed.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.670
It couldn't even pay for maintenance.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.860
Don't talk all high-and-mighty 
about the purpose of an aquarium.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.010
The attendants never shut up 
with their platitudes.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:15.560
Tingaara's fate rests with us, 
the marketing team.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.720
What is this?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.980
<b>Aquarium Tingaara Operations Manual</b>

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.980
Skim through it and get it in your head.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.450
All of this?!

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.420
The four objectives of an aquarium: 
species conservation,

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.860
environmental education, 
research and investigation, recreation.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.380
You've heard that much, haven't you?

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.690
Be mindful of the gap between the crises 
that the world recognizes

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.020
and Japan's awareness in your work.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.390
Aim to create a facility that the customers 
will want to come back to again and again.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.630
That's the best thing to do for the marine life, 
and by extension, for the employees.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:50.090
I aspire to create the top aquarium 
in the world.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.850
This has to be some kind of mistake!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:01.340
Wasn't I hired as an attendant?

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.140
You were the acting director.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.110
You'll do fine in marketing.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.860
Try new things!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.250
I can't!

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:23.980
That's her.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.910
The granddaughter of that legend.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.710
One of the girls who got pulled in 
from Gama Gama.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.200
How many of them are there? 
They practically have their own faction now.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.390
I heard she got assigned to marketing.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.290
She's not an attendant?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.230
That's a surprise.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.230
Kukuru!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.480
Kukuru!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.850
Are you alive?

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.400
I've been asked to give
you a tour of the facility.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.530
Come with me.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.290
It's even bigger than
the main tank at Gama Gama.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.300
You have to get to know Tingaara 
if you're going to settle into work here.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.710
Don't just stand there admiring it. 
Let's move on.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.580
This is the main aquarium.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.260
It's as if I'm in the ocean.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:12.870
This is the aquatic animals area.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:13.860
Kukuru!

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:18.870
Wow!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.940
They're so cute!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.150
Jeez, Kukuru.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.580
You're enjoying the aquarium 
more than anyone else here.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:32.130
Sorry, I couldn't help it.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.710
It's all right.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.370
It's important to remember 
the customers' perspective.

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.480
Let's see...

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.480
You're Nakamura Kai-kun, correct?

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.790
You're from Gama Gama, weren't you?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.700
Yes.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:47.130
And you're Higa Eiji-kun.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.550
You have a postgraduate degree, huh?

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:51.520
Yes, I suppose I do.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:55.120
The two of you will be assigned 
to Fish Team A.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.050
I'm Chief Shimabukuro.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:58.030
Nice to meet you.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.660
<b>Nanjo Marine Products</b>

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.660
<b>Frozen Fish</b>

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.160
This is the prep area.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.540
The day's worth of feed 
is in this freezer.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.420
Separate them into bags by spe—

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.170
<b>Do Not Eat</b>

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.100
Hey, who the hell put ice pops 
in the freezer?!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:16.550
Shoot!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.300
Old habits!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.520
Would you like one?

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:23.560
I would not.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:25.530
Unbelievable.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:28.190
Why would you put personal belongings 
in the feed freezer?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.280
What's wrong with some ice pops?

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:31.050
What?

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:32.570
We're at work!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.710
Of course.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:34.690
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.130
It's hard getting used to things here, huh?

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.700
I mean, Gama Gama was loosey-goosey.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.620
"Loosey-goosey," huh? Nice one.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.010
This is Tingaara.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.780
Stop setting a bad example 
for the new hires.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:49.580
Yes, sir!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.930
I'm confiscating this.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.200
The back area's huge, too, huh?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.080
There are so many rooms.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.090
Hey!

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.100
Kukuru-chan.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:06.010
This is your first day, huh, newcomer?

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.240
Are you assigned to aquatic animals?

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:08.980
Or fish, with us?

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.440
Marketing.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.650
What?!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.950
I guess that's good, too.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:21.000
Have Karin-chan whip you into shape.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.410
That's what I hope to do.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.760
Even though we're in different divisions.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.450
Don't!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.330
Jeez.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.200
May I come through, please?

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:30.140
Oh, sorry.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:38.840
You may be having fun play-working, 
but I'm desperate.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.970
Thank you for your tutelage 
way back when.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:53.230
With your help, I now work
as an attendant, just as I had hoped.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:56.080
Oh, that's right.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:58.270
I'm your senior here.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:59.820
I'll stop being so polite.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.650
Good luck in marketing.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:05.510
Bye.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.910
Yeesh.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.710
What a snob.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.290
The air's so heavy...

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.920
Welcome!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.920
This shop's so lovely.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.280
Right?

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.600
They're giving me an opportunity 
to study food as I work.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.680
What about Kamee?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.460
Mom's going to run it casually.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.520
I hope she isn't giving
her regulars any trouble.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.890
Everyone together!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:33.980
Cheers!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.010
Marketing?!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.360
It wasn't what I expected.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.970
I guess it's a huge aquarium.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.070
That's how business is.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:49.230
A lot of people work there.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:52.440
Not everyone gets what they want.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:53.360
Yeah.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:55.420
You might get reassigned someday.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.450
Don't be so down.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:02.170
You're lucky you got the job 
you wanted, Kai.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:05.740
Hey, Kukuru...

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:09.790
I was never interested 
in working at an aquarium.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:12.780
But the longer I worked at yours, 
the more I started to like it.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.930
Miyazawa-san was never involved 
in anything having to do with aquariums before.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.900
But she was working hard for us 
at Gama Gama, wasn't she?

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.150
Yeah.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.160
You might have a change of heart 
if you try something new, too.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.040
Kai...

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.200
Look at you, talking like a grown-up.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.470
I'm not a student anymore, 
starting today.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.210
"Not a student," huh?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.830
I feel so old.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.500
All right!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.920
Let's drink to celebrate our employment!

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.940
I wonder how Fuuka's doing.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.930
<b>Tingaara in the Far Away Ocean</b>

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.220
Good morning!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.440
Kukuru-san.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.430
Your cheeks are glowing as always.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:01.720
U-Um...

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.630
How do I use this?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:07.130
Oh, you tap your card here, like this.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.570
<b>Clock In</b>

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.570
<b>Clock Out</b>

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.240
That's kind of cool.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.410
Hey, Misakino!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.040
Y-Yes, sir?

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:17.660
How are the preparations for the
behind-the-scenes tour coming along?

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.240
Huh?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.670
Didn't you see it in the documents 
I handed to you yesterday?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.130
I hand documentation 
to the relevant staff beforehand.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.880
We're doing a dry run this afternoon.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.260
Check with each department 
to make sure there are no issues.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:27.800
<b>Aquarium Tingaara Operations Manual</b>

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:28.590
<b>Request for Participation 
in Behind-the-Scenes Tour Rehearsal</b>

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.760
I'm sorry! I haven't finished reading it yet.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.010
I'll be back by noon.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.160
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.770
I haven't heard anything about it.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:39.930
Look here.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.860
There was an email about it last week 
that got sent out to everyone.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.090
Really?

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.280
Kaoru, did you know about this?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.160
I guess I might have seen something.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.280
I was too busy to check my emails.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.300
Did they mention it 
in the morning assembly?

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:54.110
No, I'm not sure...

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:54.910
Marina!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.380
Yes?

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.410
Do you remember hearing about this 
in the morning assembly?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.370
Dunno.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.720
Looks like no one's heard about it.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.430
We can't have you telling us this 
out of nowhere.

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:05.820
But it's not out of nowhere.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:06.710
We sent out an email.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.670
We just opened.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.050
We're too busy getting used to work.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.270
Maybe we should put the
events off for a while.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:15.320
I agree.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.220
We can't have any issues arise.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:21.230
Could you tell that 
to the assistant director, too?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.920
May I go ahead with
preparations myself, then?

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:29.050
I know my way around back area work.

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:35.240
I'll check to make sure the routes are safe 
for our guests during off-peak hours.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:37.490
But it's happening this afternoon.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.040
I'll make it happen!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.620
I'll contact the back area staff, too.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:44.780
We'll hold the rehearsal this
afternoon, as scheduled.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.940
We won't get in anyone's way.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.110
If you insist.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.160
It's not my problem.

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:51.900
Okay!

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.000
Excuse me!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:32.320
Well, Kukuru?

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.340
Can you make it?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.620
It's all good.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:37.040
Umi-yan and Kai helped out.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.100
I got all the confirmations.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.600
Good for you.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.100
I had a change of heart 
because of what Kai said yesterday.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.130
I'm going to stop moping

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.550
about being in marketing and
try to do the work that's in front of me.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:48.610
Good for you!

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.200
Break a leg.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.700
Misakino.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:54.950
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.000
Are the dry run preparations coming along?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.660
Yes, sir.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.500
I've confirmed everything.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:01.330
Everything?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.250
Yes.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:05.710
The attendant staff seemed busy, 
so I took over.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:08.080
I'm pretty familiar with the back area.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.400
And the facilities team?

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.400
The customer staff?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:13.970
Well...

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.240
I see.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:18.010
You just did the work 
that you knew how to do.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.100
Is that right?

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:21.160
I didn't mean to...

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.730
Tingaara has a lot of employees, 
unlike Gama Gama.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.190
I'm sorry.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:29.550
But the attendant staff hadn't even 
checked their emails or anything.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:33.050
They seemed annoyed, so I figured
it'd be faster to do it myself.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.360
Get off your high horse!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.060
The rehearsal is canceled.

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:37.370
We'll reschedule.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:38.870
Yes, sir.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.020
Don't rely on your past experience.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.620
Your half-assed knowledge 
is nothing but a hindrance.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.000
You're just a newbie here.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.160
You're small fry.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:49.610
You aren't even small fry!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.100
From now on, your nickname is Plankton.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.970
I'll take Zooplankton, 
but not Phytoplankton!

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.300
What? Say that again?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:06.220
I like animal plankton like krill and stuff, 
but plant plankton just drift around! No!

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.060
I don't care!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:14.590
I don't mind some ice pops at all, 
but we did get a complaint.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:15.260
Yes, sir!

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.180
I'll be careful.

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:22.760
Um, Director?

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.200
What is it?

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.830
Did you choose Misakino-san's assignment?

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:30.800
Yes, I did.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.590
I have high hopes for Kukuru-san.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.960
High hopes?

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.840
The assistant director is very loving.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.750
I'm sure Kukuru-san will feel 
very much at home.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.850
Uh-huh...

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.310
Canceled?

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.890
I'm sorry.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.140
After all that big talk?

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.060
I'm sorry.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:56.220
Oh, yeah. Were you the one who
moved the styrofoam boxes in the hallway?

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.400
Yes.

00:18:57.710 --> 00:19:00.670
It looked like they were going to get 
in the way of the behind-the-scenes tour.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:05.620
I kept that there to store
specimen bottles and cases.

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:08.360
It's not your business. Don't touch it.

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:10.250
I'll bring them back later.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:14.550
This isn't the same aquarium 
that you were messing around at before.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.880
Get over your play-working.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.630
Are they fighting again?

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.720
Looks like it.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.690
Judging from what I've observed,

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.390
the interpersonal relationships 
at this workplace are not good.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.960
This is why I hate humans.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.490
Fish are great.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:34.260
They don't talk out of turn.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.400
By the way, do you fish?

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.160
Yeah.

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:40.900
My parents are fishermen.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.740
I think we'll get along great.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:55.120
Boss, may I borrow these technical books?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.340
Are you going to study them? 
Good for you.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:57.930
Yes.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.390
I'll read them at home.

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:02.510
I have some flexibility 
in my shifts, after all.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.510
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.380
I'm fine!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:08.260
I've always wanted this job.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.700
So I want to learn more.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.400
Want to go for dinner?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.960
I'll go home for today.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.300
I'm tired.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:21.760
Bye.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:22.970
Good work.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.800
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.530
I'm so tired.

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.820
Everything is different from Gama Gama.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:47.900
Get off your high horse!

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.640
Your half-assed knowledge 
is nothing but a hindrance.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:52.180
Get over your play-working.

00:20:56.340 --> 00:21:00.090
I've been demoted 
from First Penguin to Plankton.

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:06.060
I have to put up with nastiness 
and do work that I don't want to do.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:09.180
Is this what it means to be a grown-up?

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:17.160
I don't know that I can go on at Tingaara.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:21.880
Are you crying?

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.380
I'm not crying.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.480
I promised I wouldn't cry 
when I'm alone...

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:48.240
Long time, Kukuru!

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:51.100
Welcome back, Fuuka.
